namespace Bimwright.Dwg.Server
{
    internal static class ServerInstructions
    {
        internal const string Text =
@"dwg-mcp - MCP gateway for Autodesk AutoCAD DWG drawings. Use for current drawing metadata, layers, entity properties, simple line/circle creation, selected AutoCAD text, DBText, MText, SHX/Unicode style repair, Vietnamese translation writeback, clustered note cleanup, and DWG text rewriting.

Subagents use the parent's verified target and never switch or rebind it. If another instance/drawing is needed, report it to the parent. Inspect each host response's _target: it records the observed execution context, not the requested binding or proof of success. Drawing calls observe the locked drawing before the guard/handler; session calls observe the active drawing after the operation. A refused drawing guard can still report the observed changed drawing. Missing _target means no receipt is available; never infer it from the expected target. Treat batch receipts as context, not proof that every step succeeded or affected only that drawing.

AutoCAD routing in full mode: call dwg_list_available_targets, then dwg_switch_target(target='pid:<PID>') to verify the intended instance and active drawing before writes. Selectors also support id:acad-<year>-<PID>; an initial year 2022..2027 must be unambiguous. A different bound instance requires explicit pid:/id:; leaving a live confirmed instance requires rebind=true. One gateway keeps its PID and process start, never falls through on loss, and refuses calls pending under an older binding. Inspect dwg_get_current_target and health.target. Without rebind=true, same-process selection preserves its drawing lifetime pin, including with verify=false, which always permits reads only. expected_document_id explicitly sets the pin even without verification; verification must match it. After changing/opening drawings, inspect health and pass its intended expected_document_id or explicitly accept the new drawing with rebind=true. Failed verification preserves the prior binding. Update gateway and plugin together for target/document guards; old plugins cannot be verified for writes. Never retry a timed-out mutation without checking its outcome. ACAD_BUSY (modal dialog, active command or long operation) and QUEUE_FULL errors mean the command was not started; wait for AutoCAD to be idle, then retry.

Read-only routing: --read-only removes dwg_switch_target and blocks direct calls to it. Start the gateway with --read-only --target pid:<PID> or id:<target_id>. Initial selection occurs on the first host read/health; dwg_get_current_target reports none before that. --target does not authorize writes. On AMBIGUOUS_TARGET, TARGET_LOST or TARGET_CHANGED, use dwg_list_available_targets, then restart/reconnect the gateway with the intended explicit --target. Do not call unavailable dwg_switch_target or route to another instance automatically.

At session start select the intended target, then call dwg_health(check_updates=true) once. Routine health probes stay offline; not_checked/unknown never means up to date. Health reports host/document state and loaded server/plugin identities without requiring or locking a drawing. No target preserves gateway identity; an unsupported old plugin needs runtime observation, not a corruption warning.
Read both update.components and the full update.notification message, lookup_reason, protected_components/protected_component_reasons and unobserved_components. Follow agent_action. UPDATE_CHECK_UNAVAILABLE describes external lookup failure, not a local runtime fault or installation authorization. LOCAL_VERSION_AHEAD is informational: preserve newer components and never downgrade. Missing release revision evidence stops the update workflow, not otherwise healthy AutoCAD work. Only update_guidance.mode=prepare_update with bundle_update_proposal_allowed=true permits a release ZIP proposal and needs installation authorization; reuse existing permission. Other modes contain check/report/review only. Health never downloads packages, installs, changes client configs, saves/closes drawings or restarts processes. Never automatically replace development builds. Compare fresh initialize and tools/list runtime metadata/schema/annotations on the same reconnect with client_verification; the server cannot observe client cache refresh. Matching source revisions do not verify artifact bytes, compatibility or publisher trust.

Large output uses output_artifact: verify path/bytes/SHA-256 before reading complete JSON. scope=plugin_result precedes plugin truncation; scope=mcp_tool_result contains what the gateway received and cannot restore earlier omissions. Storage failure/size limits leave complete=false; never replay writes to recover output. Generated outputs expire after 7 days or earlier at 256 MiB/64 files; copy needed artifacts elsewhere. Per-file limit is 128 MiB. These output files are separate from opt-in call logging. Batch steps report command_ok, effective ok, outcome and unknown mutation_applied=null; prior effects can survive failure. For file output inspect file_receipt/output_verified, not command success alone.

Tools use prefix dwg_:
- Start a large-drawing read with dwg_get_drawing_profile(section='summary'). It scans all top-level model/layout entities by default; optional fifth space is all(default), model(no layout reads) or layout:<name>. Block references count once, with no block/xref expansion. Inspect source/scope, exact runtime type names, layer/space counts and completeness; observed counts or null values are not complete totals. Follow output.next_calls for types/layers/spaces with its section, offset, expected_snapshot, max_output_bytes and space. Each page rescans, without a cache; PROFILE_CHANGED requires a fresh summary. Snapshot binds scope; when changing scope omit the old expected_snapshot. Model query/count/profile ignore viewport-only changes; all/named-layout profiles and layout queries include them. Scoped replies must report scope.requested_space; an older plugin ignoring scope is refused with PROFILE_SCOPE_UNSUPPORTED. The per-result UTF-8 cap defaults to 16384 bytes (4096..65536), also subject to the global budget; it limits output, not scan time.
- Narrow entity reads with existing dwg_query_entities/dwg_count_entities, not a new tool. Original query parameters retain legacy model-space fields/order/include_geometry and limit500 clamped1..5000. New query options or paged=true select handle-ordered pages: bbox is a JSON string with min/max three-coordinate WCS drawing-unit bounds, bbox_mode is intersects(default with bbox) or contains, space is model or layout:<exact human name ignoring case>, fields is a JSON-array string from handle/type/runtime_type/layer/color_index/text/position/extents. Default fields are handle/type/layer; handle is mandatory. Do not combine include_geometry=true with new options. Bbox uses closed 3D axis-aligned GeometricExtents, not exact geometry; no INSUNITS conversion. INSUNITS0 stays unitless/unknown. No nested block/xref/viewport traversal or space fallback. Count adds only bbox/bbox_mode/space. Follow result.output.next_calls, echoing signed cursor and canonical filters/fields; limit or max_output_bytes may change, but changed filters/fields require restart without cursor. Cursor binds drawing lifetime/revision and last delivered numeric handle; invalid/tampered/stale cursors refuse. Full scan per page, no cache; output cap defaults16KiB(range4..64KiB), also subject to global budget. Inspect output omissions/has_more/blocked notes. Incomplete matching reads/extents report coverage, null exact_match_count and observed matched_count with no continuation; unsupported entity fields are null/unavailable_fields. Extended query/count are direct-tool only; gateway and plugin batch preflight refuse the entire batch before earlier items run. The gateway returns QUERY_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED for an older plugin without the feature and discards its legacy-shaped output; original-parameter reads remain available. select_by_* still returns model-space handles without pickfirst changes; use handle-only query fields for spatial handles. All four type filters accept exact managed short/full names ignoring case plus TEXT=DBText, INSERT=BlockReference, LWPOLYLINE=Polyline; do not infer extra POLYLINE types.
- Read text without pickfirst selection by adding exactly one handles(JSON-array string, empty allowed, max5000values deduplicated) or bbox(JSON-object string with min/max3) to existing dwg_get_selected_texts. Other appended options are bbox_mode(intersects/contains), space(model or layout:name), cursor and max_output_bytes(default16KiB,4..64KiB,global cap also applies). Any new option requires one explicit source. Keep MCP camelCase groupingStrength/includeEntities in next_calls. Top-level DBText/MText/MLeader and direct attributes/constant definitions only; no block/xref expansion. Full source <=5000records/8MiB UTF-8text; incomplete coverage returns no clusters/cursor, too-large source requires narrowing. Cluster complete source with unchanged spatial grouping before stable whole-cluster paging. Model snapshot ignores viewport-only changes; layout tracks them. Signed cursor binds source/grouping/includeEntities and cluster ordinal, not entity handle; parameters changing require cursor-free restart. Fit whole clusters only; inspect output.omitted_clusters/next_calls/blocked notes. Raise cap if possible or use includeEntities=false/weaker grouping/narrower source; restart when source/grouping changes. New results read_only=true/writeback_ready=false with opaque cluster_key, no writable numeric id/rewrite_mode. Source reads leave legacy rewrite groups unchanged. Translate per entity with includeEntities=true then dwg_update_texts by handle; cluster translate/collapse rewrite still requires a manual-selection read. Enhanced reads are direct only, batch/baked preflight refuse before execution. TEXT_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED discards old-plugin selection payload rather than falling back.
- query: dwg_health;  dwg_get_drawing_info, dwg_list_layers, and dwg_get_entity_properties read the current active document; the original two-parameter dwg_get_selected_texts path reads current AutoCAD pickfirst text selection and returns legacy cluster IDs for the separate writeback workflow; dwg_inspect_lisp statically scans .lsp files or inline AutoLISP for known suspicious patterns (verdict clean/caution/dangerous). No verdict certifies safety or authorizes execution.
- modify: dwg_create_layer, dwg_create_line, dwg_create_circle, dwg_attach_image, dwg_change_layer, dwg_update_texts, dwg_translate_and_rewrite, dwg_apply_unicode_style, dwg_collapse_and_rewrite write drawing/text/style changes.
- meta: dwg_batch_execute, dwg_list_available_targets, dwg_get_current_target, dwg_switch_target, dwg_list_recent_drawings, dwg_open_drawing, dwg_report_task_result, dwg_send_code, dwg_run_lisp.
- After AutoCAD work that changed a drawing or found entities the user should check, call dwg_report_task_result once before your final answer, with [label](dwg:<handle>) links to those entities; not after each tool and not for chat-only answers.
- With no drawing open: call dwg_list_recent_drawings (optional filename substring), ask the user to choose, then dwg_open_drawing with that absolute DWG path on the AutoCAD machine. Recent files may be missing; inspect exists. Both tools work without an active document and must be standalone calls, not drawing batches/baked tools. Open never saves or closes drawings. Default activate=true makes it active; read_only=true requests file read-only access but does not make the gateway tool available under --read-only. A native dialog may require the user; timeout_seconds defaults to 600 (1-900). A response/client timeout does not cancel AutoCAD work; inspect state before retrying.
- view: Start visual reading with dwg_capture_view_image (inline image plus JSON). If region_navigation.supported, choose a normalized top-left-origin rectangle on that image and call dwg_inspect_view_region with its capture_id. Inspect the new image before deciding the next region. Keep ancestor capture IDs and use dwg_restore_view to return to an overview. Use each newly returned ID for further navigation. Do not interpret a failed image_delivery as a failed zoom: take a smaller fresh capture. Region navigation is limited to one top-down, unrotated, orthographic model-space viewport. Verify inferred labels/dimensions against CAD text and entity data. Do not claim unseen regions have been reviewed.
- optional toolbaker, when enabled: dwg_list_baked_tools, dwg_run_baked_tool, dwg_list_bake_suggestions, dwg_accept_bake_suggestion, dwg_dismiss_bake_suggestion, dwg_create_bake_issue_draft.
- dwg_send_code is on by default; --disable-send-code removes it and blocks batch dispatch. --read-only also removes it. The AutoCAD MCPDISABLECODE command disables it for the session (MCPENABLECODE re-enables only the host gate, not the server setting).
- dwg_run_lisp is a compatibility refusal: all execution is blocked at server and plugin until an enforceable isolation/trust policy exists. MCPENABLECODE does not unblock LISP. Do not bypass refusal through send_code, batch, ToolBaker, or reformatted payloads. send_code remains full-trust C#, not a sandbox or machine-wide malware protection.

General CAD tools operate on the current AutoCAD active document. Entity arguments use AutoCAD hex handles returned by selection, creation, or property tools.
Before text writeback, manually select text and call dwg_get_selected_texts using only its original groupingStrength/includeEntities parameters. Explicit-source read-only clusters cannot authorize writeback. Read-only mode permits queries, selection and standalone view zoom, but no drawing edits or file output. Capture, region inspection and view restore write image files and are unavailable in read-only mode.";

    }
}
